// Span-only fixture (ast-source-spans slice 1): a non-ASCII character on a
// line before a target field's declaration. Proves `SourceSpan.start`/`end`
// are UTF-16 code-unit offsets, not raw UTF-8 byte offsets — `é` is 2 UTF-8
// bytes but 1 UTF-16 code unit, so a byte-offset span for `title` would be
// off by one relative to the correct UTF-16 offset.
//
// Deliberately excluded from the golden-snapshot parity loop
// (`packages/compiler/test/parity.mjs`) — it carries no
// `fixtures/snapshots/22-non-ascii.json`, since its only purpose is the
// span/slicing assertions in `parity.mjs`'s dedicated span block and the
// Rust unit test in `crates/indigo-compiler/src/span.rs`.

Table Post {
  id Int @id
  @note("café")
  title String
}
